  "findings": [
    "Both nine-case arms complete, all case controls/finite/bounds pass, integrity pass with no problems. Exact original coarse/half reproduction; exact repeated common/own quarter case.",
    "Network common-state neural-only refinement changes responses about1881x more than outer-only phasewise,1800x phase-mean. Starting-state effect is material but smaller than neural-step effect in this test.",
    "Peptide common-state neural-only changes about78x more than outer-only phasewise,75x phase-mean. Coarse anchor effect is about15x common-state neural-only, so independent settled/phase state is a dominant contributor for this selected model/test. Ratios compare separate maxima, not a causal variance decomposition.",
    "Successive common-state joint phase-mean differences network:0.0001493018,0.0001000588,0.0000485841; peptide:0.00000722764,0.00000369081,0.00000186172. Shrinking differences support convergence tendency, not proof finest level meets full-domain tolerance.",
    "Network RIVL->RMDVL common-state phase mean grows0.0002554524 to0.0005533971 from coarse to eighth; quarter->eighth difference is about8.78% of finest value, not an error bound.",
    "Peptide RMDR->RMDL own-state mean changes sign from-0.0000630108 coarse to+0.0000109398 half to+0.0000480033 quarter. Common-state means stay positive across tested clocks; anchor dependence matters."
